                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. Corrosion occurs when a metal undergoes oxidation, usually through natural contact with oxygen in the air or contact with moisture, especially water containing electrolytes. Metals tend to lose electrons (oxidation), so many metals corrode over time. Metals can be protected against corrosion in several ways, including covering its surface with paint or another substance or having a layer of surface oxidation. Also, a sacrificial anode made from a metal that is more reactive and more likely to corrode can be connected to the metal needing protection against corrosion."
